// The magnetic field of a bar magnet, schematic. Proportions are invented, NOT measured data.
// Proof of concept for the item register (docs/item-output-bar.md); not for lessons as it stands.
// The field lines are drawn from a simple model: the magnet is treated as two point poles (north at x = +3.6, south at x = -3.6), and each
// line follows the direction of the combined field from the north pole until it comes back to the magnet. Directions are correct for that
// model; the spacing of the lines shows strength only roughly (five lines, each copied six times round the axis). Real magnets have
// more complicated fields near their ends, and the field continues through the inside of the magnet (not drawn). Lines are in the xy plane and
// are then turned about the x axis. Units are cm. Colours: north red, south blue, field lines yellow; they are named in the captions only.
